{pad:meta title='Stockroom: how it works'/}

<div class="work-help">
  <div class="work-head">
    <div>
      <h2>Stockroom, built in PAD</h2>
      <p>A stock register with receipts and issues, an immutable movement journal, reorder planning, valuation charts and printable shelf labels.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Try a complete workflow</h3>
    <p>Add an item, receive its opening stock, then issue some units. Try issuing more than are available. Set its reorder level above the remaining stock and check the reorder report and shelf labels.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Pages</h3>
    <div class="work-table-wrap">
      <table class="work-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Page</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?index">index</a></td>
            <td>Search stock and filter the items that need reordering.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?new">new</a></td>
            <td>Create an item, with unit cost and reorder level.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?movements">movements</a></td>
            <td>Filter, sort and page through the movement journal.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?reports">reports</a></td>
            <td>Calculate reorder quantities and stock value by category.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><a href="?labels">labels</a></td>
            <td>Print A4 shelf labels or use the printable subsystem PDF link.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>The template is the application</h3>
    <p>There are no PHP page controllers or application PHP helper libraries. Each page declares its own form rules, reads requests through PAD helpers, makes workflow decisions with PAD tags, binds database values, and renders its result. The only PHP files configure the application and enter PAD.</p>
    <pre><code>&#123;pad:array &quot;category, sum(stock*unit_cost)/100.0 as value from items group by category&quot;, toData=&#x27;valuation&#x27;/&#125;
&#123;chart:donut data=&#x27;valuation&#x27;, label=&#x27;category&#x27;, value=&#x27;value&#x27;, title=&#x27;Stock value in EUR&#x27;/&#125;</code></pre>
    <p>Database reads use <code>pad:array</code>, <code>pad:record</code> and <code>pad:field</code>. A <code>toData</code> store connects queries to charts, tables, calendars and printables. Reusable layout slots, flash messages, fragments and the shared theme switcher complete the interface.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Data integrity</h3>
    <p>A single conditional INSERT checks that an issue leaves enough stock. A SQLite trigger applies the movement in the same transaction, and the stock column has a nonnegative constraint. A unique request key prevents the same form submission from changing stock twice. Item settings use a version check. Unit costs are stored as integer cents; valuation uses the current unit cost, not historical accounting cost.</p>
    <p>Forms carry CSRF tokens. Literal <code>rules=</code> declarations run on the server before <code>padPosted()</code> returns true; <code>client</code> adds browser feedback from the same rules. Successful writes redirect before rendering. Search values are bound as data and output is escaped.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="work-panel">
    <h3>Storage and scope</h3>
    <p>The first visit creates <code>DATA/stockroom/stockroom.sqlite</code> from <code>apps/stockroom/_install/schema.sql</code>, including fictional starter records. Changes persist across visits and browser sessions. Keep that database when updating the application.</p>
    <p>This is one shared workspace for everyone who can access this installation. It does not provide user accounts or separate customer workspaces. All workflows work without application JavaScript; PAD's controls add progressive enhancements.</p>
  </section>
</div>
